    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7c4ab439_9da3dd19",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/DeviceStateMonitor.java",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 294,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-19T23:24:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, this one is not about power consumption... it\u0027s trying to discourage people from spamming the API when there\u0027s really no need. At vehicular speeds anything more than tower ID isn\u0027t going to be very helpful for tracking, and at lower speeds you don\u0027t need it every 2 seconds. :-) I think this is something we can keep tuning, but when we do I\u0027d like to consider whether the requester is the foreground app or possibly using the SystemApi (LocationProvider) to exempt them from these restrictions if need-be. Thus, I prefer the default behavior to be pretty restrictive.",
      "parentUuid": "8141815b_bd5ca645",
